{
  "id": "lesson-yarn-npm-006",
  "slug": "versioning-semver",
  "title": "Versioning and SemVer",
  "description": "Understand semantic versioning, lockfiles, and version resolution.",
  "order": 6,
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedMinutes": 8,
  "tags": [
    "npm",
    "yarn",
    "package-manager",
    "fundamentals"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Semantic Versioning (SemVer) ensures predictable updates. Both NPM and Yarn interpret version ranges using caret (^) and tilde (~) notation."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "text": "SemVer Format",
        "level": "h2"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A SemVer version has three parts: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH. Breaking changes increment MAJOR, features increment MINOR, and bug fixes increment PATCH."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": [
          "Range",
          "Example",
          "Matches"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Exact",
            "1.2.3",
            "Only 1.2.3"
          ],
          [
            "Caret",
            "^1.2.3",
            ">=1.2.3 <2.0.0"
          ],
          [
            "Tilde",
            "~1.2.3",
            ">=1.2.3 <1.3.0"
          ],
          [
            "Any",
            "*",
            "Any version"
          ],
          [
            "Hyphen",
            "1.2.3 - 2.3.4",
            "Range inclusive"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "text": "Lockfiles",
        "level": "h2"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Lockfiles (package-lock.json or yarn.lock) pin exact versions. Always commit lockfiles to version control."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "language": "bash",
        "caption": "Generate a lockfile",
        "code": "npm install\n# or\nyarn install"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "info",
        "title": "Best Practice",
        "text": "Never edit lockfiles manually. Regenerate them with the install command."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "SemVer",
            "definition": "Semantic Versioning: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH."
          },
          {
            "term": "Caret",
            "definition": "^ allows minor updates."
          },
          {
            "term": "Tilde",
            "definition": "~ allows only patch updates."
          },
          {
            "term": "Lockfile",
            "definition": "Pins exact installed versions."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "faq-block",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          {
            "question": "What if a package violates SemVer?",
            "answer": "Use overrides or resolutions to force a specific version."
          },
          {
            "question": "Should I use exact versions?",
            "answer": "Lockfiles handle this. Keep ranges flexible in package.json, pinned in lockfiles."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "SemVer defines MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH."
          },
          {
            "text": "Caret and tilde control update ranges."
          },
          {
            "text": "Lockfiles ensure reproducible installs."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "moduleSlug": "yarn-npm-fundamentals",
  "courseSlug": "yarn-npm-packages"
}
